<article class="env-lemma" id="03QR">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03QR">Lemma <span data-tag="03QR">58.2.2</span>.</a> Let $K$ be a field. Let $K^{sep}$ be a separable closure of $K$. Consider the profinite group $G = \text{Gal}(K^{sep}/K)$. The functor </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \begin{matrix}  \text{schemes étale over }K 

&  \longrightarrow 

&  G\textit{-Sets} 

\\  X/K 

&  \longmapsto 

&  \mathop{\mathrm{Mor}}\nolimits _{\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(K)}(\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(K^{sep}), X) 

\end{matrix}  \]
</div>
  <p> is an equivalence of categories. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      A scheme $X$ over $K$ is étale over $K$ if and only if $X \cong \coprod _{i\in I} \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(K_ i)$ with each $K_ i$ a finite separable extension of $K$ (Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/02GL" data-tag="02GL">29.37.7</a>). The functor of the lemma associates to $X$ the $G$-set 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \coprod \nolimits _ i \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _ K(K_ i, K^{sep})  \]
</div>
    <p>
       with its natural left $G$-action. Each element has an open stabilizer by definition of the topology on $G$. Conversely, any $G$-set $S$ is a disjoint union of its orbits. Say $S = \coprod S_ i$. Pick $s_ i \in S_ i$ and denote $G_ i \subset G$ its open stabilizer. By Galois theory (Fields, Theorem <a href="/tag/0BML" data-tag="0BML">9.22.4</a>) the fields $(K^{sep})^{G_ i}$ are finite separable field extensions of $K$, and hence the scheme 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \coprod \nolimits _ i \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}((K^{sep})^{G_ i})  \]
</div>
    <p>
       is étale over $K$. This gives an inverse to the functor of the lemma. Some details omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>